{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויצוהו כאשר דבר ה' ביד משה", :translit "viyitzavhu ka'asher diber Hashem beyad Moshe", :gloss "And he charged him, as YHWH spoke by the hand of Moses"} {:he "שלא לבטל תורה ותמיד מפני המלחמה", :translit "shelo levatel Torah v'tamid mipnei hamilchamah", :gloss "not to nullify Torah and the daily offering on account of war"} {:he "פרשת תמידין", :translit "parashat tamidin", :gloss "passage of the daily offerings"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut parashiyot): the immediately following passage of daily offerings (Num 28–29) is read as a consequence of Moses' charge to Joshua."}], :frame {:text "The Sages address Joshua's charge here. Sifrei Zuta 140 understands 'as YHWH spoke by the hand of Moses' to include the command that public Torah study and the daily offering must not be suspended even during wartime. The juxtaposition of the daily-offerings passage immediately after (Numbers 28:1–8) is cited by Sifrei Zuta as the textual basis for that obligation.", :sources ["Sifrei Zuta 140"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut parashiyot): the immediately following passage of daily offerings (Num 28–29) is read as a consequence of Moses' charge to Joshua.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:31:57.502728697Z", :model "glm-5.2"}